		},
		{
			"id": "112888543055600394",
			"parentId": "112888431344169500",
			"url": "https://mas.to/@jamesdoc/112888543034130095",
			"author": {
				"name": "James Doc",
				"url": "https://mas.to/@jamesdoc",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/409/738/484/481/647/original/1e7b209847b7fbae.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-01T20:01:05.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> That is one of the hardest questions in serverless.</p><p>Serverless framework doesn't need the paid element; it's a yml config which sets up lambda, deploys, etc. You can trigger it locally, or through a GitHub action, etc.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112888556243381933",
			"parentId": "112888543055600394",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112888556243381933",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-01T20:04:27.286Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mas.to/@jamesdoc\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jamesdoc</span></a></span> ah yeah—I’m currently in the “I have a production project that is costing more than I’d like due to usage levels and I want to try to reduce costs” phase</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112888787313946861",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112888787313946861",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-01T21:03:13.143Z",
			"content": "<p>in order to upload a file to amazon you need to create an s3 bucket, sure.</p><p>the one thing we know for sure is that uploads over 10MB will tax the amazon upload process beyond scalable comprehension</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112888788335991783",
			"parentId": "112888787313946861",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112888788335991783",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-01T21:03:28.738Z",
			"content": "<p>in order to use that file from your bucket in your lambda as a layer it needs to be in the same aws region, sure.</p><p>the one thing we know for sure is that servers are not allowed to communicate outside of their municipality</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
