			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> just so I understand this: you’ve historically used paid-for services which deploy to AWS for you? There is a useful middle ground between this and using SAM and the AWS sdk directly; stuff which runs on your machine. (Apologies if this is condescendingly obvious and you know it!) I used to use sls, but they increasingly want you to use their service: instead, I recommend architect at <a href=\"https://arc.codes\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">arc.codes</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a>. It’s nice, and the team (<span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>brianleroux</span></a></span>, <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@macdonst\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>macdonst</span></a></span>) are helpful :)</p>",
